A paint server in object bounding box units on a <tspan> or <textPath>
maps onto the box of the whole <text> element in Ladybird, and getBBox()
still reports the <tspan>’s own box. Chrome 158, Firefox 151, and WebKit
26.5 all render it that way: for fills, strokes, radial gradients, and
patterns, and for a nested <tspan>, a <tspan> in a <textPath>, a filled
<textPath>, and a <tspan> on a line of its own. In Blink, SVGResources::
ReferenceBoxForEffects() swaps an SVG inline for the <text> it finds
with LayoutSVGText::LocateLayoutSVGTextAncestor(). In WebKit, the box
RenderSVGInline::objectBoundingBox() returns is its RenderSVGText
ancestor’s. And in Gecko, SVGUtils::GetBBox() swaps a frame in a text
subtree for its closest SVGTextFrame, unless getBBox() asked for the
TextContentBounds of the frame itself.
